          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            When the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+of+open+subsets"} lattice of open subsets
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            is the primordial example of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            then its dual
            %em
              lattice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets"} closed subsets
            is the primordial example of a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong co-Heyting algebra
          %p
            In general, co-Heyting algebras are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            to Heyting algebras and like them come equipped with non-Boolean logical operators that make them interesting players in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+logic"} modal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paraconsistent+logic"} paraconsistent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linguistics"} linguistics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum+physics"} continuum physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+theory"} quantum theory
            and in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mereology"} mereology
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong co-Heyting algebra
            is a bounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            equipped with a binary
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtraction"} subtraction
            operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo \
                  %mo :
                  %mi L
                  %mo ×
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \backslash :L\times L\to L
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo \
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\backslash y\leq z
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\leq y\vee z
            %sup#fnref:1
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          %p
            A
            %strong bi-Heyting algebra
            is a bounded distributive lattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            that carries a Heyting algebra structure with implication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            and a co-Heyting algebra structure with subtraction
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo \
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \backslash
          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Co-Heyting algebras were initially called
                %em Brouwerian algebras
                \. Bi-Heyting algebras were introduced and studied in a series of papers by Cecylia Rauszer in the 1970s who called them
                %em semi-Boolean algebras
                which suggests to view them as a generalization of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebras
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                such that the lattice
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sub(X)
                of subobjects is a bi-Heyting algebra for every object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in\mathcal{E}
                is called a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-Heyting+topos"} bi-Heyting topos
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The lattice of closed subsets of a topological space is a co-Heyting algebra with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo \
                        %mi Y
                        %mo =
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∩
                            %msup
                              %mi Y
                              %mi c
                          %mo ¯
                        %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\backslash Y=\overline{X\cap Y^c}\quad
            %li
              %p
                A Boolean algebra provides a (degenerate) example of a bi-Heyting algebra by setting
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\Rightarrow y:=\neg x\vee y
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo \
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\backslash y:=x\wedge\neg y
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreflexive"} irreflexive
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison"} comparison
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
                or a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+poset"} enriched poset
                on the co-Heyting algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\op
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                is the Heyting algebra of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo \
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash b=0
                iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo \
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash b\leq 0
                iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∨
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\leq b\vee 0
                iff
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\leq b
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash a=0
            %li
              %p
                As _
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo \
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \backslash x
                has a right adjoint it preserves colimits hence:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo \
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∨
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo \
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a\vee b)\backslash x =(a\backslash x)\vee (b\backslash x)\quad
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo \
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi a
                      %mo \
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash 0\leq a\backslash 0
                iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo \
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\leq 0\vee (a\backslash 0)
                iff
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\leq a\backslash 0\quad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\leq 0\vee a
                and the adjunction yield
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi a
                        %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash 0\leq a\quad
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mi a
                        %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash 0 = a\quad
            %li
              %p
                Suppose
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\leq b\vee x
                then
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mi b
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash b\leq x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo \
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi a
                      %mo \
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash b\leq a\backslash b
                follows
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∨
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\leq b\vee (a\backslash b)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo \
                        %mi b
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi a
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\backslash b =\Wedge\{x|a\leq b\vee x\}\quad
            %li
              %p
                The subtraction operation permits to define the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+negation"} co-Heyting negation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∼
                        %mo :
                        %mi L
                        %mo →
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim: L\to L
                %em non a
                in Lawvere (1991), by setting
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mo \
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim a:=1\backslash a
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
                in turn can then be used to define the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+boundary"} co-Heyting boundary operator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo :
                      %mi L
                      %mo →
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial :L\to L
                by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial a:=a\wedge\sim a
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial a
                is not necessary trivial is dual to the non-validity of the
                %em tertium non datur
                for general Heyting algebras and points to the utility of co-Heyting algebras for
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paraconsistent+logic"} paraconsistent logic
            %li
              %p
                In
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-Heyting+toposes"} bi-Heyting toposes
                like e.g.
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+subtoposes"} essential subtoposes
                of presheaf toposes (
                %a{:href => "#Law91a"}> Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "#Reyes"} Reyes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image+functor"} inverse image functors
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+re+and+de+dicto"} de re and de dicto
                effects. The parallel between this and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutator"} commutator
                in quantum mechanics has been suggested by Lawvere thereby somewhat anticipating the view of Döring (2013).
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+negation"} co-Heyting negation
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Heyting+boundary"} co-Heyting boundary
            %li
